Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:07:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] trystero: a connection's end names the connection, and
 a room acts only on its own

A room heard every connection's end by the peer alone, so a late end of a connection it was no longer bound to dropped a peer bound to a live one, without detaching it: the connection stayed open with no binding and no idle timer, and the pair never met again. room_endpoint::connection_ended now takes the connection that ended, the app passes the one its slot names, and a binding tells whether it is on a connection by its owner, which a connection made at a freed address does not share.
